    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0468" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.13/22.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 21, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You may at an opportune time discuss the matter reported in your telegram of
                    November 19 with the President of Cuba if he seems inclined to approve the bill,
                    pointing out this Government’s views in the sense of the Department’s telegram
                    of January 6, 1913, 7 p.m. The bill appears to have substantially the same scope
                    as the one of December 16, 1912; in this connection you are referred to the
                    Department’s telegrams of March 5, 7, 12 and 18, 1913.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
